## One rule concern

`scripts/blog-source-audit.mjs` treats `youtube` as a `VENUE_WORD` with no `OUTLETS` entry for self-published channels, so a first-party video grades **VAGUE** however precisely it's cited. The two Army slots now carry title + exact date + channel and still read VAGUE. The grader's actual ask — a fact-checker can get from text to tape — is satisfied; the tag can't move without editing the script's `OUTLETS` table. I left the script alone and flagged it in the draft rather than working around it.

